Filtering and Pagination

  Collection endpoints take query parameters.  An optional filter narrows the list.  Pagination limits how
  much is returned.  This tutorial shows both, and both together.

  A collection read has no branching pipeline, so it stays a single function.  This is the read side of the
  {{{../SpringRestCrudHttpServer/index.html}CRUD Orchestration}} pattern, where the write side is composed
  of many functions but the list is not.

  {{{https://github.com/officefloor/OfficeFloor/tree/master/tutorials/springboot/SpringRestFilterHttpServer}Tutorial Source}}


